@startuml integration-contract
!pragma layout smetana
title Browser-to-backend integration contract

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Customer or staff member" as user
component "React screen\nApp + child components" as ui
component "Frontend API client\napi.ts" as client
rectangle "HTTP JSON boundary\n/api/machine" as http
component "MachineController\nSpring MVC routes" as controller
component "MachineService" as service
component "VendingMachine\nIn-memory business state" as machine
component "MachineExceptionHandler\nRFC 9457 responses" as errors

user --> ui : clicks a screen control
ui --> client : calls an operation
client --> http : sends JSON over HTTP
http --> controller : maps method and path
controller --> service : passes typed request values
service --> machine : runs business rules
machine --> service : state, receipt or refund
service --> controller
controller --> http : JSON success response
http --> client
client --> ui : validates and returns data
machine ..> errors : throws a machine error
controller ..> errors : validation or body error
errors --> http : 4xx/5xx problem+json
http --> client : stable code and detail
client --> ui : ApiError shown as a banner

note top of http
GET   /api/machine
  -> MachineView: credit, stock, coins, revenue
POST  /api/machine/credit {amount}
  -> MachineView
POST  /api/machine/credit/return
  -> {returned}
POST  /api/machine/purchase {items}
  -> PurchaseResult: total, change, receipt
POST  /api/machine/refill {items}
  -> MachineView
end note

note bottom of errors
Error replies use application/problem+json.
The stable code (for example INSUFFICIENT_STOCK)
lets the frontend identify the problem without
trying to read meaning from the detail text.
end note

note bottom of machine
The frontend cart is only a request.
The backend checks stock, credit and capacity
again before changing machine state.
end note
@enduml
